(57138, 1939, 'header-sub-title', 'The Chinese government has historically adopted currency controls over the outflow of the Reminbi (“RMB”), particularly in relation to implementation measures for cross-border M&A capital flows. Such policies are principally designed to stabilize the RMB in the international currency markets and maintain the balance of China’s capital accounts.\r\n'),
